Sītā bids Hanumān rest one day to ease her grief --- Sītā fears death and deeper grief after his departure --- Sītā doubts hosts or princes can cross the hard ocean --- Sītā says only Garuḍa wind and Hanumān can leap sea --- Sītā demands glorious rescue killing Rāvaṇa not stealth befitting Rāma --- Hanumān says Sugrīva resolved with mind-swift unhindered monkeys --- Hanumān claims none lesser than him and mightier hosts wait --- Hanumān promises Laṅkā gate princes on his back roaring hosts and Ayōdhyā crowning
